{"id": "unknown-2026-08-31-006", "date": "2026-08-31", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 36, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["growth"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India Q1 real GDP grows 7.8% as GVA rises 8.2%", "content": "India’s real GDP is estimated to have grown 7.8 per cent year on year in Q1 FY 2026-27, while nominal GDP rose 10.3 per cent.\nReal GVA growth of 8.2 per cent and higher goods and services trade indicators offer demand signals for manufacturers, exporters and sourcing teams.\nMoSPI’s next quarterly GDP release, covering Q2 FY 2026-27, is scheduled for November 30, 2026.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-q1-real-gdp-grows-7-8-as-gva-rises-8-2--313094-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-08-31-007", "date": "2026-08-31", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 36, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India pushes TRAs towards industry-led, outcome-driven textile R&D", "content": "Ministry of Textiles held the second TRA coordination meet to make India’s textile R&D more industry-led, collaborative and outcome-based.\nDiscussions covered technical textiles, Centres of Excellence, New Age Fibres, startups, funding, skills, governance and i-TRAMS mapping.\nTRA plans for 2026–27 will target testing, standardisation, commercialisation, import substitution and MSME solutions.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-pushes-tras-towards-industry-led-outcome-driven-textile-r-d-313093-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-08-31-008", "date": "2026-08-31", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 36, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Indonesia building wastewater treatment plant for SMEs in Kalimantan", "content": "Indonesia is constructing a wastewater treatment plant in Tapin Regency using green technology for SMEs in south Kalimantan. \nThe facility, being built under the Industrial Technology Enhancement Partnership Fund programme, will allow traditional Sasirangan textile SMEs to reuse around 90 per cent of treated wastewater, boosting operational efficiency while maintaining environmental sustainability. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/indonesia-building-wastewater-treatment-plant-for-smes-in-kalimantan-313091-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-08-31-009", "date": "2026-08-31", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 36, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["cotton_price"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["increase"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "DTY nylon 6 firms: How far will feedstock costs push it?", "content": "Chinese nylon 6 DTY filament yarn prices moved modestly higher from August 26 to 28, 2026, as crude-linked feedstock costs rose.\nNaphtha gained about 3.7 per cent and benzene about 2.5 per cent, ahead of caprolactam's 0.61 per cent rise and nylon 6 chips' 0.80 per cent increase.\nDTY pass-through was uneven: 40D/36F rose 0.76 per cent, 70D/24F 0.33 per cent and 50D/24F stayed flat.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/dty-nylon-6-firms-how-far-will-feedstock-costs-push-it--313086-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-08-31-010", "date": "2026-08-31", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 36, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Pakistan BCI cotton's 2.70% jump could tighten regional yarn costs", "content": "Pakistan’s KCA spot rose 2.70 per cent on Tuesday after flood damage in Punjab and Sindh, then stayed unchanged through Friday.\nIndia’s Shankar-6 traded flat at INR 199 per kg, supported by comfortable surplus supplies.\nChina’s 3128B fell to CNY 18,527.28 per tonne on Thursday, rebounded 0.53 per cent on Friday and rose 0.82 per cent on August 31.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/pakistan-bci-cotton-s-2-70-jump-could-tighten-regional-yarn-costs-313083-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-08-31-011", "date": "2026-08-31", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 36, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Tk 30,000 wage demand could raise Bangladesh’s SS27 risk", "content": "Bangladesh’s garment sector is entering its first minimum-wage review under a shortened three-year cycle, with unions seeking reconstitution of the Minimum Wage Board. \nThe last structure took effect in December 2023, pointing to a new one by December 2026 under the amended labour law. \nRMG exports were US$39.35 billion in FY2024-25, up 8.84 per cent, with an 81.49 per cent share of total exports. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/tk-30-000-wage-demand-could-raise-bangladesh-s-ss27-risk-313074-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-08-31-012", "date": "2026-08-31", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 36, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "26-point duty gap could favour flexible apparel sourcing", "content": "A rebuilt United States tariff structure is shifting apparel sourcing from choosing one country to moving between several quickly. \nIndia’s PDS Limited and Indonesia’s Busana Apparel Group have announced a non-binding alliance across six manufacturing locations. \nNew Section 301 duties create a landed-cost gap that could favour CAFTA-DR apparel from Honduras and Nicaragua. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/26-point-duty-gap-could-favour-flexible-apparel-sourcing-313069-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
